// Two Go services in one repository, developed together and deployed apart.
//
// Committed on purpose. Without it every Go command has to be run from inside
// one service's directory, which is how the documented commands drifted into
// `go run ./server` — a form that never worked from anywhere, because the
// module root was `server/` itself. With the workspace, `go test frameplayer/...`
// from the repository root covers both services, and each keeps its own
// `go.mod` so a container built from one service's directory (where there is no
// workspace file) resolves exactly the same dependencies.
//
// Note the pattern: **`frameplayer/...`, not `./...`**. The repository root is
// not itself a module, so a path pattern rooted there matches nothing and says
// so in a way that reads like a broken workspace ("directory prefix . does not
// contain modules listed in go.work"). A module-path pattern has no such
// problem and covers both by their shared prefix.
go 1.24

use (
	./services/relay
	./services/tmdb
)
